.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-release-bump-unusable 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-release\-bump\-unusable \- Move a burned or stray\-tagged version to the next one in all four release paths, as one commit on the release branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten release bump\-unusable\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-branch\fR> <\fB\-\-changelog\fR> <\fItag\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Move a burned or stray\-tagged version to the next one in all four release paths, as one commit on the release branch
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-branch\fR \fI<branch>\fR
The release branch the bump is committed onto
.TP
\fB\-\-changelog\fR \fI<changelog>\fR
The changelog carrying the release\*(Aqs `## [X]` section
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fItag\fR>
The release\*(Aqs tag
